  "question": "Does the company publish a channel for reporting product vulnerabilities?",
  "method": "For each of the 68 companies in datalake/bci-landscape.json: fetch RFC 9116 security.txt at /.well-known/ and the site root (with and without www), and the paths /security, /product-security, /vulnerability-disclosure, /responsible-disclosure, /security-policy, /trust and /en/security. A page counts only if it answers 200, is not the homepage, and its title names security, vulnerability or disclosure. Every candidate, and every site that did not answer cleanly, was reviewed by hand. Parent-company channels count where the parent sells the tracked product line.",
  "limits": "A channel hosted at another path, behind a contact form, or on a third-party platform can be missed. 'none_found' means none was found by this method on this date, not that none exists. Companies are invited to send corrections.",
